WEBVTT

00:01:30.710 --> 00:01:34.040
The following tale is a work of pure fiction.

00:01:34.050 --> 00:01:37.850
<b>August 1581 {ts}</b>

00:01:34.050 --> 00:01:37.850
<b>Inaba Province {ts}</b>

00:01:34.050 --> 00:01:37.850
<b>Hashiba Hideyoshi's Main Camp {ts}</b>

00:01:59.310 --> 00:02:05.540
Should we seal this route, neither a mouse or horse shall pass.

00:02:05.540 --> 00:02:10.110
Once we've severed this supply route, their demise is all but certain.

00:02:11.270 --> 00:02:14.520
General Hashiba seems troubled as of late.

00:02:15.410 --> 00:02:17.550
He speaks not a word.

00:02:22.100 --> 00:02:27.980
I would have ye reign to realize my ambition.

00:02:29.290 --> 00:02:30.440
General Hashiba. {moushi agemasu}

00:02:30.440 --> 00:02:33.990
General Takayama Ukon has arrived from Settsu.

00:02:42.330 --> 00:02:44.830
<b>Strategic Incitation {ts}</b>

00:02:46.940 --> 00:02:48.460
I am Takayama Ukon. {takayama ukon}

00:02:48.460 --> 00:02:52.680
Milord's orders are to assist General Hashiba in the siege of Tottori Castle.

00:02:56.030 --> 00:02:59.490
I come with fresh supply of steeds from Milord as well.

00:02:59.490 --> 00:03:00.450
Much obliged. {gokurou}

00:03:02.780 --> 00:03:05.480
General Hashiba Hidenaga has arrived as well.

00:03:08.040 --> 00:03:11.480
Your sister is wedded to General Takayama, aye?

00:03:11.480 --> 00:03:12.920
Aye.

00:03:12.920 --> 00:03:14.700
You have much to converse over.

00:03:14.700 --> 00:03:16.600
Do keep your brother company. {teicho ni motenashi shitekure}

00:03:18.240 --> 00:03:21.470
General Hashiba has not the leisure of time.

00:03:21.990 --> 00:03:24.680
'Tis a fine cream coat.

00:03:29.750 --> 00:03:31.740
'Tis the hot brand of overlapped rings! {until yakiin}

00:03:32.250 --> 00:03:35.260
Authentic steeds of the Ise Province!

00:03:35.990 --> 00:03:41.760
Its rigid spine and muscular loins are shaped to perfection! {from gyutto until yoi}

00:03:42.560 --> 00:03:47.970
I believe the besieged desire that horse more so than ye, Brother.

00:03:48.450 --> 00:03:53.400
Without supplies or food, they shall be starved into submission.

00:03:53.400 --> 00:03:57.430
To the starved, horses and rations of straw would be a welcome sight.

00:03:58.240 --> 00:04:00.990
Woe, for compassion is forsaken in war.

00:04:01.450 --> 00:04:05.020
Compassion shall lead the deaths of more innocents. {until umidashi kanemasen}

00:04:08.680 --> 00:04:10.770
Have ye faith in God the Father, Brother?

00:04:12.810 --> 00:04:16.760
I have faith in a trio of higher powers.

00:04:20.720 --> 00:04:22.140
My faith...

00:04:22.510 --> 00:04:25.470
Were one to attain all three tea jars, {until naraba}

00:04:25.470 --> 00:04:30.390
'twould signify the unconditional wresting of rule.

00:04:30.390 --> 00:04:34.900
One may rule the country with three such tea jars?! {until aru no ka}

00:04:34.900 --> 00:04:41.470
'Tis the Nitta, Hatsuhana, and Narashiba tea jars.

00:04:43.180 --> 00:04:45.080
belongs to three tea jars.

00:04:58.840 --> 00:05:06.220
Was this the rebellious urge Matsunaga and Araki had succumb to? {until ajiouta no darou}

00:05:08.770 --> 00:05:10.530
Three months have passed.

00:05:11.050 --> 00:05:13.230
My disciple, shall ye fulfill my ambition?

00:05:13.230 --> 00:05:16.730
Though you are one of the Three Tea Masters, {until to iedo}

00:05:16.730 --> 00:05:21.110
I shall take your head for any mention of usurping Milord.

00:05:21.610 --> 00:05:24.110
My head is yours to take.

00:05:26.870 --> 00:05:34.630
My ambition opposes the ambition of Milord. {until aiiremasenu}

00:05:35.050 --> 00:05:40.630
With might, Milord shall usher the nation into a gaudy era.

00:05:43.000 --> 00:05:49.100
I, with aesthetics, shall usher the nation into an era of refinement.

00:05:49.100 --> 00:05:52.940
I devote the remainder of my life to this ambition.

00:06:26.850 --> 00:06:32.430
Milord trusts in those who exhibit no deceit in their eyes.

00:06:33.270 --> 00:06:35.350
However, my trust is not easily gained. {daga ore wa chigau}

00:06:35.940 --> 00:06:40.430
Depending on the efforts exhausted, men may conceal deceit.

00:06:41.480 --> 00:06:43.490
However, hands may conceal naught.

00:06:43.930 --> 00:06:49.580
One's hands may reveal the entirety of their life. {all the way until sarakedasu}

00:06:53.000 --> 00:06:59.200
Master Senno's hands are rigid, feeble, and afflicted by chilblains.

00:07:00.470 --> 00:07:04.420
They are not hands of a deceitful, nor foolish, man.

00:07:05.770 --> 00:07:06.930
Then...

00:07:12.410 --> 00:07:15.000
A man may live to fifty years...

00:07:15.000 --> 00:07:17.930
but none are immune to death. {messenu mono wa arubeki ka}

00:07:21.910 --> 00:07:24.490
There exists none who are immune to death!

00:07:25.780 --> 00:07:29.990
I shall share your ambition, Master Senno.

00:07:31.540 --> 00:07:37.130
I assess others only after they present adequate authenticity and knowledge of their wares.

00:07:38.000 --> 00:07:43.560
Had Master Souji intended deceit, I would have discerned it.

00:07:43.560 --> 00:07:50.510
Indeed, Milord's current influence is akin to possessing all three tea jars, though he possesses two.

00:07:50.920 --> 00:07:51.740
Aye. {umu}

00:07:53.760 --> 00:07:57.270
Beheld ye both tea jars?

00:07:58.010 --> 00:08:00.630
Prior, I had no knowledge of their existence.

00:08:01.330 --> 00:08:06.280
Milord had only displayed wares he deemed as significant treasures.

00:08:06.280 --> 00:08:09.840
As a disciple to Master Senno in tea brewery,

00:08:10.270 --> 00:08:13.040
I know the origins of these tea jars.

00:08:17.300 --> 00:08:23.550
The Nitta tea jar was once held by the heroic descendant of the Genji clan, Nitta Yoshisada, {from nitta katatsuki unto kara}

00:08:23.550 --> 00:08:29.430
and passed unto the founder of tea brewery, 
Murata Jukou, who praised its magnificent beauty.

00:08:30.540 --> 00:08:35.350
The Hatsuhana tea jar was once held by Consort Yang Guifei, {until youkihi ga mochi}

00:08:35.350 --> 00:08:40.950
and passed unto the eighth Ashikaga Shogun, 
Ashikaga Yoshimasa, who praised its refreshing beauty.

00:08:42.500 --> 00:08:48.410
And lastly, the Narashiba tea jar now held by tea master Shimai Soushitsu of Hakata. {until narashiba katatsuki}

00:08:48.820 --> 00:08:54.950
Once held by Shogun Ashikaga Yoshimasa as well, he praised its entrancing amber hue.

00:08:54.950 --> 00:08:59.200
Milord's desire for the Narashiba tea jar
must exceed his own ambition.

00:09:01.320 --> 00:09:06.230
Milord possesses the near entirety of the nation's masterpieces.

00:09:06.980 --> 00:09:11.890
Perhaps Milord may wrest rule with an aesthetic mindset, rather than force. {until narimasukarana}

00:09:15.350 --> 00:09:23.100
Were I to liquidate all of my assets, I would still be denied a single lid of the tea jars.

00:09:23.490 --> 00:09:27.290
Men possess gifts not akin to one another, Brother.

00:09:27.290 --> 00:09:32.060
The only difference between the men worthy and unworthy of possessing masterpieces

00:09:32.060 --> 00:09:34.530
are the gifts bestowed upon them by God. {until itashikatagozaimasen}

00:09:34.900 --> 00:09:40.710
What must I accomplish to attain even one of the three?

00:09:47.590 --> 00:09:52.460
I bestow upon thee a holy cross,
praying thou shalt commit no sin for greed. {from sono tame until agemashou}

00:09:55.540 --> 00:09:58.140
'Tis an intriguing shape...

00:09:58.140 --> 00:10:00.950
Merely the shape?

00:10:07.650 --> 00:10:13.100
At present, only Hidenaga knows of our plot.

00:10:13.100 --> 00:10:16.660
I ask ye to refrain from writing and visiting my quarters as well.

00:10:17.120 --> 00:10:23.160
I am concerned as to whether or not the loyal General Akechi will assist in our plot.

00:10:26.170 --> 00:10:29.670
Leave your displeasure unspoken.

00:10:30.070 --> 00:10:33.170
I shall sway his loyalty.

00:10:35.180 --> 00:10:38.410
And what of my other disciple, Governor Furuta?

00:10:38.410 --> 00:10:41.350
He shall be useful.

00:10:41.350 --> 00:10:46.560
Should he refuse, my vassal, his father, shall serve as my hostage. {until touzen da}

00:10:47.250 --> 00:10:54.570
As I am deeply intrigued by Governor Furuta,
I ask ye to do him no harm. {until nasaimasu you ni}

00:10:56.700 --> 00:10:59.830
Make way for General Hashiba Hidenaga! {until mon wo ake}

00:11:02.640 --> 00:11:05.430
I shall leave the recruitment entirely to you.

00:11:05.430 --> 00:11:09.920
I shall often inform General Hidenaga of 
General Akechi's movements as well.

00:11:09.920 --> 00:11:10.700
Farewell. {dewa}

00:11:18.850 --> 00:11:20.600
Was that Senno Soueki?

00:11:21.720 --> 00:11:22.900
Mad, are ye?

00:11:22.900 --> 00:11:25.290
A tea master ne'er wears armor!

00:11:25.290 --> 00:11:28.370
Neither does a tea master brew on the battlefield.

00:11:29.770 --> 00:11:32.960
Though, I do recall a man of such stature...

00:11:43.290 --> 00:11:47.000
Curse your own foul fortunes...

00:11:49.980 --> 00:11:54.050
Men, be rid of those insolent fools.

00:11:54.050 --> 00:11:54.690
Aye! {ha}

00:12:05.500 --> 00:12:08.970
Indeed, a magnificent steed.

00:12:08.970 --> 00:12:09.970
Be mine... {hoshii}

00:12:28.410 --> 00:12:32.330
for I curse my own unbridled ambition.

00:12:38.970 --> 00:12:42.760
<b>December 1581 {ts}</b>

00:12:38.970 --> 00:12:42.760
<b>Omi Province Azuchi Castle {ts}</b>

00:12:44.080 --> 00:12:48.980
No longer shall I refer to ye as "Bald Rodent," but as "Baldy!"

00:12:48.980 --> 00:12:53.170
I am pleased to have ascent from the status of a beast.

00:12:53.170 --> 00:12:54.610
Aye, Baldy. {sasuga wa hage}

00:12:54.610 --> 00:12:56.810
Only a man may know the mind of another!

00:13:00.100 --> 00:13:03.610
Ye've done well to capture both Tottori Castle and Awaji Island. {until yokuzo otoshita}

00:13:03.610 --> 00:13:06.130
I award ye eight masterpieces!

00:13:07.180 --> 00:13:09.130
'Tis a hanging scroll of perched sparrows...

00:13:09.130 --> 00:13:11.110
a celadon flower vase...

00:13:11.110 --> 00:13:12.780
an Asakura tea jar...

00:13:13.390 --> 00:13:15.550
a Tenmoku-glazed tea bowl of Daikaku Temple... {until chawan}

00:13:16.020 --> 00:13:18.110
a Tenmoku-glazed tea stand of Amagasaki... {until tenmokudai}

00:13:19.270 --> 00:13:20.920
a tea scoop, crafted by Master Shutoku... {until chashaku}

00:13:20.920 --> 00:13:22.480
a tong crafted by Master Tetsu...

00:13:22.480 --> 00:13:24.140
and a tea bowl of the Joseon Kingdom!

00:13:31.270 --> 00:13:32.600
I wish to devour them.

00:13:33.760 --> 00:13:39.980
I shall consume their essence and savor each piece within!

00:13:42.990 --> 00:13:44.070
Ye shan't have any.

00:13:46.580 --> 00:13:51.340
Milord advised I exhibit these to evoke your humorous emotions, {until iwaretaga}

00:13:51.340 --> 00:13:53.260
but dare ye mad to consume them?

00:13:53.260 --> 00:13:54.080
Aye? {nou}

00:13:55.000 --> 00:13:56.940
Please behave, Milord. {mou hidesama}

00:13:58.480 --> 00:14:03.490
Lady Nene would be saddened should she learn of your lechery.

00:14:03.490 --> 00:14:07.620
Ye know not of the efforts I've exhausted in war.

00:14:07.620 --> 00:14:12.860
Were my exhaustion to be soothed by one woman or another, Nene would pardon my actions. {from onago to yurushitekureruwa}

00:14:12.860 --> 00:14:15.980
Milord, General Akechi has returned to his residence.

00:14:18.910 --> 00:14:20.770
I have yet to assess them. {mada jikkuri mitoran}

00:14:20.770 --> 00:14:23.240
Return them to their vessels afterwards.

00:14:26.940 --> 00:14:29.310
I shall relinquish one of those eight to General Akechi.

00:14:29.310 --> 00:14:33.140
Bring me the most modest amongst the eight.

00:14:33.140 --> 00:14:34.750
Very well.

00:14:54.520 --> 00:14:56.570
'Twas three days ago.

00:14:57.040 --> 00:14:58.020
{skip NIKA}

00:14:58.650 --> 00:15:05.040
That day, when had I delivered persimmons from Mino to Azuchi Castle in preparation for the new year, {from nobunagasama e until ano hi}

00:15:05.040 --> 00:15:07.290
'twas then that I overheard this matter.

00:15:07.780 --> 00:15:13.040
Milord had bestowed these eight masterpieces unto General Hashiba.

00:15:14.910 --> 00:15:18.090
General Hashiba has not a discerning eye, {until minukemaite}

00:15:19.170 --> 00:15:24.570
therefore, my impeccably handmade tea scoop shall suffice for the original.

00:15:39.090 --> 00:15:41.710
Long has it been, General Akechi.

00:15:45.710 --> 00:15:52.110
As I owe much for your dispatching reinforcements from the sea to Tottori Castle, {until soraeba}

00:15:52.110 --> 00:15:55.080
I've come to express my gratitude this day.

00:15:56.860 --> 00:16:00.310
'Tis a pleasant surprise, though caught ill-prepared.

00:16:00.310 --> 00:16:02.090
Please, do not trouble yourself.

00:16:05.960 --> 00:16:09.980
Has the war council determined the course of action against Takeda Katsuyori?

00:16:11.340 --> 00:16:17.970
Aye, but perhaps I've taken excessive leisure with caution when formulating stratagems.

00:16:17.970 --> 00:16:21.730
Milord often chides my ineptitude for decisiveness.

00:16:22.290 --> 00:16:23.980
How I do envy you.

00:16:25.780 --> 00:16:30.710
I recall every single time Milord had reprimanded me.

00:16:30.710 --> 00:16:34.070
I even recall the reprimands of others as well.

00:16:34.070 --> 00:16:41.750
In fact, General Akechi, you have the misfortune to be chided by Milord more so than any other. {from soreyue until gozaru}

00:16:48.470 --> 00:16:52.470
I do so empathize with Milord's decisions.

00:16:52.470 --> 00:16:57.610
However, he vents only his anger and reprimands strictly unto his generals.

00:16:58.230 --> 00:17:02.650
Milord sings no praises for your valiant actions.

00:17:02.650 --> 00:17:05.660
Nay, General Hashiba has surely received less praise...

00:17:06.500 --> 00:17:13.370
Though Milord may chastise me for my indirection, I bear him no grudge.

00:17:19.820 --> 00:17:25.590
Though ye bear no grudge, the same may not be said of your clan.

00:17:27.590 --> 00:17:31.730
I've felt naught but restlessness through recent eves, {until nemurasenanda}

00:17:31.730 --> 00:17:34.940
concerned for my clan's posterity. {until omoimasutona}

00:17:36.600 --> 00:17:41.950
Though we both contend to capture Kyuushuu for ourselves, {until soregashi ni seyo}

00:17:41.950 --> 00:17:45.610
would it not also fall under the control of Milord's clan?

00:17:48.300 --> 00:17:55.860
Within my clan, there are voices of displeasure over this matter.

00:17:58.370 --> 00:18:04.390
Perhaps Milord desires the Oda clan to rule sovereignly over this nation.

00:18:04.390 --> 00:18:09.920
What would Milord dirty ourselves for, following the capture of Kyuushuu?

00:18:13.550 --> 00:18:16.380
His time has already passed.

00:18:16.860 --> 00:18:20.230
My vision for this nation is rebirth.

00:18:21.110 --> 00:18:26.820
There is no rebirth, should old men of his competence continue to rule.

00:18:28.140 --> 00:18:30.650
Only men of my era shall reign almighty.

00:18:32.490 --> 00:18:35.870
For your contributions, he shall remain unharmed.

00:18:36.660 --> 00:18:40.270
Nobutada, Nobukatsu, and Nobutaka!

00:18:41.570 --> 00:18:44.080
Ye marched stout with honor before the Emperor.

00:18:44.990 --> 00:18:47.140
Indeed, 'tis most proper of my sons.

00:18:47.640 --> 00:18:49.290
I shall gift unto thee.

00:19:01.970 --> 00:19:05.710
He would have us wage war to the shores of the Ming and Joseon Dynasties. {until meijirare}

00:19:05.710 --> 00:19:10.570
Though our clans perish in those wars, the Oda clan shall remain intact. {until antai no mama}

00:19:11.340 --> 00:19:18.440
Should we return as defeated men, a life in exile alike Sakuma Nobumori may await.

00:19:20.530 --> 00:19:26.300
For what reason do we devote ourselves to his ambition? {until nouu}

00:19:27.210 --> 00:19:32.940
Though I pass beyond 45 years of life, I feel naught but exhaustion

00:19:32.940 --> 00:19:35.590
when reminded of the meaningless contention between our clans for fame. {from shojiki}

00:19:41.350 --> 00:19:45.780
How I yearn to be as a child once more,
 and frolic in the fields...

00:19:46.770 --> 00:19:51.900
Though I be mad for such fantasy, should I reach my final years, {from musou until aru no nara}

00:19:51.900 --> 00:19:54.860
I desire to live as a man of tea brewery.

00:19:55.950 --> 00:19:57.190
Had I one wish though...

00:20:04.450 --> 00:20:09.460
'twould be to serve a virtuous man alike yourself.

00:20:18.270 --> 00:20:21.090
Do forget my shameful sight.

00:20:21.090 --> 00:20:25.950
Were my warriors to behold this sight, 'twould drain their morale.

00:20:30.350 --> 00:20:34.610
This masterpiece is but a modest gift.

00:20:35.020 --> 00:20:43.120
Should I perish in battle, it shall serve as a memento. {from moshi soregashi until kudasare}

00:20:43.580 --> 00:20:44.710
General Akechi...

00:20:47.770 --> 00:20:48.700
farewell.

00:21:19.830 --> 00:21:22.660
A ploy to shed tears under pain of a blade.

00:21:22.660 --> 00:21:24.950
Though Akechi Mitsuhide is a man of sound repute, {from ikani}

00:21:24.950 --> 00:21:26.880
he must have acknowledged my message.

00:21:27.490 --> 00:21:32.220
Were my incitation lackluster to commit him to treason,

00:21:32.620 --> 00:21:34.670
another ploy remains.

00:21:51.760 --> 00:21:54.200
'Tis a masterpiece only in name.

00:21:54.660 --> 00:21:56.840
A modest gift, indeed.

00:22:03.790 --> 00:22:06.070
Most unusual...

00:22:07.210 --> 00:22:10.700
Though I've gathered a fair few wares of virtue,

00:22:11.710 --> 00:22:17.860
my presence has yet to be requested at tea ceremonies.

00:22:21.540 --> 00:22:25.170
Once Milord holds absolute control over the nation,

00:22:25.170 --> 00:22:27.780
great battles shall cease to be fought.

00:22:28.840 --> 00:22:32.520
To be allowed attendance to a tea ceremony, I must succeed the rank of messenger, {until dai daimyou ni naru ni wa}

00:22:32.520 --> 00:22:37.020
and become a true governor of fiefdoms through achievements in battle. {from wazuka until nakarou}

00:22:41.880 --> 00:22:47.240
I am aroused through my eagerness for success. {until okoshiteshmatta ka}

00:22:52.860 --> 00:22:53.910
Osen?

00:22:54.770 --> 00:22:56.130
Where art thou? {osen ya}

00:24:34.560 --> 00:24:36.220
<b>Next! {ts}</b>

00:24:46.650 --> 00:24:48.320
<b>She possesses a discerning eye! {ts}</b>

00:24:56.540 --> 00:24:59.860
<b>Topple Takeda {ts}</b>
